  "worked_solution": "First, because the initial condition is $y(-3)=1,$ we fill $y=1$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{\u2032}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =-x+5y \\\\  & =-(-3)+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $\u0394y$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & ={y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $24$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
